# A new candidate in Typesense 30.2, a clock effect (RESULTS.md, finding 3). After a backward
# step of the wall clock by 120 s before step 20, a pause of the leader at step 30 leaves the two
# other nodes without a leader for 68 s, until the leader goes on: no node starts an election.
# braft's election timer is a repeating bthread timer, and its next run is a wall-clock time
# (src/braft/repeated_timer_task.cpp, schedule; brpc's TimerThread reads gettimeofday). The run
# that was due when the clock went back comes 120 s late. Without T= the same pause gets a new
# leader, and final_available holds.
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=none | run T=20:-120 P=nodes.primary@30+25
